0</Value><Unit>ms</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Applied only if "ResetPhoneAfterXmlUpload" is enabled. If the phone is reset and it needs extra time to settle before continuing, then this param should have a greater than zero value.</Description><Constraints>100</Constraints></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>XML Upload Fail Action</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Designates what to do if XML Upload fails.</Description><Constraints>Display Message Box=0;Notify Through Error Window=1;Throw Exception=2;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Request EFS Sync</Name><Value>1</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>258</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>File path to Sync</Name><Value>/</Value><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request EFS Sync</ParentName><Description>Source file path</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>EFS Sync Timeout</Name><Value>10</Value><Unit>Seconds</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request EFS Sync</ParentName><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Delay before sending diag command</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>milli-Seconds</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request EFS Sync</ParentName><Description>Delay before sending the Diag command - Sync to EFS.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Number of Retries</Name><Value>3</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request EFS Sync</ParentName><Description>Number of retries in case the first attempt to sync to EFS fails. 
Enter '0' for disabling retries.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Watch for Messages ?</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Text Marker</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Any Text to Log - Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "format" part of printf. Supported printf place-holders are: %d,%f,%s; for int, double, and string. There can be many place-holders. Example entry: Marker :: c:\qcn_backup\%s. In this example "%s" will be replaced with the corresponding or equivalent key value in "Args" parameter and it will result in the corresponding marker in the log.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Marker Args</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><Description>Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "args" part of printf. A delimited list of keywords. Must have the same number of elements as the number of place-holders in "Command" param. Example entry: TESTTREEID. In this example "TESTTREEID" key will replace the "%s" found in "Command" param with the actual TESTTREEID of the tree used.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use Config Lookup For Marker Args</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><DisplayHint>1282</DisplayHint></ParameterCls></Parameters><HIVENodeProperties>0</HIVENodeProperties></HiveProperties></HiveTest><FolderProperties NodeType="FolderProperty"><UniqueName /><UniqueNames /><AxiomMetricCSV /><LogPath /><isAxiomEdit>false</isAxiomEdit><Expanded>true</Expanded><TestName>Static NV</TestName><Re