aType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>258</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Write or Read?</Name><Value>1</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>0=Read, 1=Write</Description><Constraints>Read=0;Write=1;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Save Read Value</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>valid only for NV Read, the value will be saved in memory and later NV write node can use it to rewrite to phone.</Description><DisplayHint>258</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use Read Value to Write</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>valid only for NV Write, the previously cached NV read value will be used instead the strings configured in this node</Description><DisplayHint>258</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Delete Saved Read Value After Write</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>valid only for NV Write, the previously cached NV read value will be deleted from memory do avoid stale usage.</Description><DisplayHint>258</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Multi-Phone</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Click to see the options for multiple active phone settings.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Primary Phone Technology</Name><Value>-1</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Multi-Phone</ParentName><Description>Valid only for multiple active phones concurrency, when Multi-phone has been added by CheckPhoneCommAndPhoneMode or AddActivePhone node. if multiple active phones were detected on comports and added by AddActivePhone, this flag decides which phone is the primary phone. -1 is auto detect, based on the name of DLL.</Description><Constraints>SameAsDLLName=-1;CDMA=0;WCDMA=1;GSM=2;BlUETOOTH=3;MEDIAFLO=4;DVBH=5;ANALOG=6;GPS=7;ISDBT=8;1xEVDO=9;LTE=10;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Request EFS Sync</Name><Value>1</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>258</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>File path to Sync</Name><Value>/</Value><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request EFS Sync</ParentName><Description>Source file path</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>EFS Sync Timeout</Name><Value>10</Value><Unit>Seconds</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request EFS Sync</ParentName><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Delay before sending diag command</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>milli-Seconds</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request EFS Sync</ParentName><Description>Delay before sending the Diag command - Sync to EFS.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Number of Retries</Name><Value>3</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request EFS Sync</ParentName><Description>Number of retries in case the first attempt to sync to EFS fails. 
