</Notes><NodeRID>-1</NodeRID><NumberOfTests>1</NumberOfTests><Parameters><ParameterCls><Name>Calibration Configuration Name</Name><Value>RFCAL_GSM</Value><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Apply Supplemental Loss</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Set this flag to add supplemental loss to cal offsets.</Description><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Supplemental Loss DB File Path</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Apply Supplemental Loss</ParentName><Description>Supplemental Loss DB full file path</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Watch for Messages ?</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Text Marker</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Any Text to Log - Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "format" part of printf. Supported printf place-holders are: %d,%f,%s; for int, double, and string. There can be many place-holders. Example entry: Marker :: c:\qcn_backup\%s. In this example "%s" will be replaced with the corresponding or equivalent key value in "Args" parameter and it will result in the corresponding marker in the log.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Marker Args</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><Description>Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "args" part of printf. A delimited list of keywords. Must have the same number of elements as the number of place-holders in "Command" param. Example entry: TESTTREEID. In this example "TESTTREEID" key will replace the "%s" found in "Command" param with the actual TESTTREEID of the tree used.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use Config Lookup For Marker Args</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><DisplayHint>1282</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable DLF Logging</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>File Name Marker</Name><Value>TEST</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><Description>File Name will be DLFLog_&lt;filenamemarker&gt;_TimeStamp.dlf. File will be stored in C:\Qualcomm\Qdart\Temp</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>List of Log Packets for DLF Logging</Name><Value>0x5082,0x5260</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls></Parameters><HIVENodeProperties>0</HIVENodeProperties></HiveProperties></HiveTest><HiveTest NodeType="Test"><Index>36d52e04-954a-407c-be9d-309c69aedac0</Index><OriginalIndex>454420dd-fed6-4636-b6de-27d84e7670fa</OriginalIndex><HiveProperties NodeType="TestProperty"><UniqueName /><UniqueNames /><AxiomMetricCSV /><LogPath /><isAxiomEdit>false</isAxiomEdit><TestName>RFCal Init : GSM</TestName><RealName>RFCal_V2_Init</RealName><Description>Initializes the test equipment for RFCal under the given "Technology".

