</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Tx Antenna Path Selection</Name><Value>65535</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Specify which Tx antenna path to calibrate. Use only with Set Device and SigPath version V1.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Set Device and SigPath</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Set Device and SigPath
.If this flag is enabled, the Set Device and SigPath API will be called with the RF_PATH_INFORMATION obtained from DUT</Description><Constraints>False=0;V1=1;V2=2;V3=3;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA Calibration</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>DA Calibration ITEMS ROOT</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Perform DA Calibration</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if DA calibration should be performed</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use List Mode Power if available</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>On boxes that support list mode power, enabling this flag will cause the measurement to be done using the GPRF Power List Measurement</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:NV Mappings</Name><Value>1,2,3</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Maps the measurements from this node to specific NV tables. 1 = F1, 2 = F2, 3 = F3</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Step Duration</Name><Value>250</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: Time Intervals. Controls how long the RGI is held at the same value by the UUT. A segment length of 1 corresponds to 3.692 microsecs, which is 1 Time Interval.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:PA Ranges</Name><Value>0,1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Controls Tx PA gain settings for which measurements will be performed. Should be only one value per each range to be actually calibrated. </Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Waveform Max Level</Name><Value>30</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: dBm. The max level in the waveform (per PA range) - used to set input level on the box</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Trigger RGI</Name><Value>31</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Trigger RGI - RF Gain Index for the trigger segment</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Trigger PA Range</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Trigger PA Range - PA Range for the trigger segment</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Start RGI</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Start RGI - First segment RGI</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Stop RGI</Name><Value>27</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Stop RGI - Last segment RGI. (May be skipped depending on the start,stop combination)</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Step RGI</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Step RGI - The sweep steps by "step rgi"</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Measurement Start Delay</Name><Value>300</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: mS. The delay between arming the test equipment and the phone. Default: 0 ms.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Measurement Offset</Name><Value>200</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: uS. It delays "DA:Measurement Length" from taking effect once trigger occurs. Default: 112 us.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Measurement Length</Name><Value>500</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: uS. Controls how long of each segment is measured.Default: 250 uS. Do not go lower as since some equipment may not support.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Saturation Detection Window</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: dB. Applied to GMSK maxPower of PA Range 0. Example 1: Measured Power List PA0 [...,29,31,32.25,32.4,32.5] and window is 0.3, NV will be [...,29,31,32.25,32.25,32.25] Example 2: Measured Power List PA0 [...,29,31,32.25,33.4,33.8] and window is 0.3, NV will be [...,29,31,32.25,33.4,33.8]</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:TCXO Setting</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Can be used to fine tune the frequency of the tx signal within the channel.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Insert RGI0 step after entering new PA Range</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>If Yes, inserts an extra RGI0 step after every PA change</Description><DisplayHint>5378</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Insert RGI0 step every PA change</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>If Yes, inserts an extra RGI0 step before every PA change</Description><DisplayHint>5378</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Output File to Append GSM Tx DA Char Data</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Complete file name with path for GSM Tx DA Characterized data table generation. Leave empty to NOT generate GSM Tx DA Char Data.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Limits</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>DA Calibration Limits</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Expected Min Trigger Power</Name><Value>23</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Limits</ParentName><Description>Sanity Check: Expected Min Trigger Powers. Calibration will fail if trigger falls below this.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Expected Max Trigger Power</Name><Value>38</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Limits</ParentName><Description>Sanity Check: Expected Max Trigger Power. Calibration will fail if trigger exceeds this.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Min Expected GSM Power List</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Limits</ParentName><Description>Min limit list on measured GSM power in a given PA range. Should be one value per each range to be actually calibrated. If empty no limits will be applied</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Max Expected GSM Power List</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Limits</ParentName><Description>Max limit list on measured GSM power in a given PA range. Should be one value per each range to be actually calibrated. If empty no limits will be applied</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Min Expected EDGE Power List</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Limits</ParentName><Description>Min limit list on measured EDGE power in a given PA range. Should be one value per each range to be actually calibrated. If empty no limits will be applied</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DA:Max Expected EDGE Power List</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Limits</ParentName><Description>Max limit list on measured EDGE power in a given PA range. Should be one value per each range to be actually calibrated. If empty no limits will be applied</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Temp Comp Adjust</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>DA Calibration</ParentName><Description>Temp Comp Adjustment</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable Temp Comp NV Write Only</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Temp Comp Adjust</ParentName><Description>If enabled, writes current UUT temperature to NV. No adjustment of DA cal data is performed during RF calibraiton.</Description><DisplayHint>5378</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable Temp Comp Adjustment</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Temp Comp Adjust</ParentName><Description>Adjust Temp Comp based on the Thermal ADC Values measured during DA Calibration</Description><DisplayHint>5378</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Thermal ADC alpha</Name><Value>0.5</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Temp Comp Adjust</ParentName><Description>The percentage of the delta between  (A) thermal ADC read before TxLin and (B) thermal ADC read after TxLin,				   to be used for determining the equivalent calibration temperature. The equivalent calibration temperature= A + alpha * (B - A)</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>HighThermalADCLimit</Name><Value>1250</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Temp Comp Adjust</ParentName><Description>The highest thermal ADC that will disable this tempComp Adjust feature</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>LowThermalADCLimit</Name><Value>990</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Temp Comp Adjust</ParentName><Description>The lowest thermal ADC that will disable this tempComp Adjust feature</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>PreDist Calibration</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Pre Distortion Calibration ITEMS ROOT</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Perform PreDistortion Calibration</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if Predistortion calibration for high power EDGE should be performed.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Swapped Order - EDGE First</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Set to true if calibration waveform has EDGE First. Default : false</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Log PreDistortion Calibration Data</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if Predistortion calibration for high power EDGE should be performed.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>PreDist:NV Mappings</Name><Value>1,2,3</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Maps the measurements from this node to specific NV tables. 1 = F1, 2 = F2, 3 = F3</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>PreDist:PA Range</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Controls Tx PA gain settings for which measurements will be performed. Should be only one value to be actually calibrated. </Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>PreDist:Waveform Max Level</Name><Value>35</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: dBm. The max level in the waveform (per PA range) - used to set input level on the box</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>PreDist:Preceding DC Duration</Name><Value>625</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: quarter symbols. Duration of the preceding dc length in the calibration waveform</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>PreDist:EDGE Duration</Name><Value>625</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: quarter symbols. Duration of the edge waveform in the calibration waveform</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>PreDist:Power of Calibation RGI</Name><Value>26</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: dBm. Predistortion calibration has to be performed at an RGI that corresponds to this Power.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>PreDist:Calibration RGI List When DA Calibration Skipped</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>If DA Calibration is skipped these RGIs are used to generated the predistortion calibration waveform. Calibration is repeated &amp; logged once for value in this list.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>PreDist:Measurement Start Delay</Name><Value>50</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: mS. The delay between arming the test equipment and the phone. Default: 0 ms.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>PreDist:TCXO Setting</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Can be used to fine tune the frequency of the tx signal within the channel.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>PreDist:DC Transient Duration</Name><Value>60</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>%, As a percentage of DC Duration. Range 10 to 60%</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>PreDist:Number of Transient Skip Symbols in EDGE Duration</Name><Value>90</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Number of Transient Skip Symbols in EDGE Duration. Range &gt; 0, Range &lt; 100</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Override Smoothing Defaults?</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Override Smoothing Parameters?</Description><DisplayHint>5378</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable AMAM Smoothing?</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Override Smoothing Defaults?</ParentName><Description>Enable AMAM Smoothing?</Description><DisplayHint>5378</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>AMAM Smoothing Knot</Name><Value>2</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Override Smoothing Defaults?</ParentName><Description>AMPM Smoothing Knot</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>AMPM Smoothing Knot</Name><Value>2</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Override Smoothing Defaults?</ParentName><Description>AMPM Smoothing Knot</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>PreDist Modem Constants OverRide</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if Modem constants need to be overriden. This should be left at disabled for targets that precede NikeL based ones.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></Parame