s><Name>NonIQPreDist:Power of Calibation RGI</Name><Value>26.5</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: dBm. Predistortion calibration has to be performed at an RGI that corresponds to this Power.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Warmup Correction Factor</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: dB. Compensation factor to account for transient droop in cal waveform.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Phase Slope Compensation Factor</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: degrees/10dB. Compensation factor to account for transient droop in cal waveform - in degrees/10 dB of input power</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Power Slope Compensation Factor</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: dB/10dB. Compensation factor to account for transient droop in cal waveform - in dB/10 dB of input power</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:AMAM Smoothing Knot</Name><Value>2</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>AMAM Smoothing Knot, unit dBDAC. An input to the spline smoothing function</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:AMPM Smoothing Knot</Name><Value>2</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>AMPM Smoothing Knot, unit dBDAC. An input to the spline smoothing function</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Calibration RGI When DA Calibration Skipped</Name><Value>25</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>If DA Calibration is skipped this RGI is used to generated the predistortion calibration waveform</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Step Duration</Name><Value>200</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: Time Intervals. Controls how long the DAC is held at the same value by the UUT. A segment length of 1 corresponds to 3.692 microsecs, which is 1 Time Interval.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Measurement Offset</Name><Value>112</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: uS. It delays "DA:Measurement Length" from taking effect once trigger occurs. Default: 112 us.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Measurement Length</Name><Value>100</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: uS. Controls how long of each segment is measured.Default: 250 uS. Do not go lower as since some equipment may not support.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Trigger DAC List</Name><Value>10000</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>List of Trigger DACs, these form the beginning of the waveform and are not used as measurements</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Measurement DAC List</Name><Value>10000</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>List of Measurement DACs. Note: This list must be monotonic - increasing or decreasing.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Phase Reference DAC</Name><Value>10000</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Phase refernce DAC, which will be interleaved in the waveform</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Min Limit of Max Power</Name><Value>27</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Sanity Check: Minimum Limit of Max Power measured in the calibration waveform</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Min Limit of power flatness of Adjacent Phase Reference Steps</Name><Value>0.5</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Sanity Check: Min Limit of power flatness of Phase Reference Steps</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Phase Spike Detection Threshold (degrees)</Name><Value>10</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Sanity Check: Max limit of phase between measurment steps (if larger - calibration will fail)</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQ PreDist Modem Constants OverRide</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if Modem constants need to be overriden</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Modem Const:DAC Scaling</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Modem Constants OverRide</ParentName><Description>Digital Gain Unity parameter used to process captured IQ Data</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Dump Debug CSV</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Creates a csv file for Non IQ Cal debug. File saved as C:\NonIQDebug.csv.File format is DAC, F1 AMAM,F1 AMPM, F2 AMAM, F2 AMPM, F3 AMAM,F3 AMPM</Description><DisplayHint>5378</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use Debug CSV to create NV instead of measured data</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Uses file C:\NonIQDebug.csv to generate AMAM/AMPM NV.File format is DAC, F1 AMAM,F1 AMPM, F2 AMAM, F2 AMPM, F3 AMAM,F3 AMPM</Description><DisplayHint>5378</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>EnhLinTx Calibration</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Enh Tx Lin Calibration ITEMS ROOT</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Perform Enh Lin Tx Calibration</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if Enh Lin Tx calibration should be performed. This includes DA Calibration  and charachterized predistortion calibration specified as rgi list, pa, mode list. </Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Use List Mode Power if available</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>On boxes that support list mode power, enabling this flag will cause the measurement to be done using the GPRF Power List Measurement</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:NV Mappings</Name><Value>1,2,3</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Maps the measurements from this node to specific NV tables. 1 = F1, 2 = F2, 3 = F3</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Step Duration</Name><Value>50</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: Time Intervals. Controls how long the RGI is held at the same value by the UUT. A segment length of 1 corresponds to 3.692 microsecs, which is 1 Time Interval.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Waveform Max Level</Name><Value>30</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: dBm. The max level in the waveform (per PA range) - used to set input level on the box</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Calibration PA Range</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Predistortion calibration will be done at this PA range.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Power of Calibation RGI</Name><Value>26.5</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: dBm. Predistortion calibration has to be performed at an RGI that corresponds to this Power.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:PA Ranges List</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Controls Tx PA gain settings for which measurements will be performed. Should be only one value per each segment to be actually calibrated. </Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:RGI List</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Controls Tx RGI gain settings for which measurements will be performed. Should be only one value per each segment to be actually calibrated. </Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Mode Param List</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Controls Mode settings for which measurements will be performed. Should be only one value per each segment to be actually calibrated. Modes 0,1 will be used for DA Cal, rest for Char Predistortion cal.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Measurement Start Delay</Name><Value>50</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: mS. The delay between arming the test equipment and the phone. Default: 0 ms.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Measurement Offset</Name><Value>50</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: uS. It delays "DA:Measurement Length" from taking effect once trigger occurs. Default: 112 us.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Measurement Length</Name><Value>100</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: uS. Controls how long of each segment is measured.Default: 250 uS. Do not go lower as since some equipment may not support.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Saturation Detection Window</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: dB. Applied to GMSK maxPower of PA Range 0. Example 1: Measured Power List PA0 [...,29,31,32.25,32.4,32.5] and window is 0.3, NV will be [...,29,31,32.25,32.25,32.25] Example 2: Measured Power List PA0 [...,29,31,32.25,33.4,33.8] and window is 0.3, NV will be [...,29,31,32.25,33.4,33.8]</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Modem Const:DAC Scaling</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Digital Gain Unity parameter used to process captured IQ Data</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Do Power Adaptation</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if power adaptation should be applied during calibration. This will automatically be disabled if there are no enhanced sweep points.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Do Piecewise-Linear Adaptation</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if piecewise linear adaptation should be applied during calibration.This will automatically be disabled if there are less than two enhanced sweep points.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Do Slope Correction</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if slope correction should be applied during calibration.This will automatically be disabled if there are less than two enhanced sweep points.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Slope Correction Align Low</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>When applying slope correction, set this to Enable to align the curve at the low side. Otherwise, the curve will be aligned at the high side.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Do Max Power Estimation</Name><Value>1</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if extrapalating max power estimation should be applied during calibration. </Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Output DA Char to Output File</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if char DA will be written to the char XML output file.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Output File to Write GSMTxChar Data</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Complete file name with path of the GSM Tx Characterized data table genration. Use %s to specify the UUTID, %d to specify the current date, and %t to specify the current time. When generating characterization data, normal predistortion calibration (including NV writes) will be partially disabled. Leave empty to NOT generate GSM Tx Char Data and run normal calibration instead. When filenames are the same (minus timestamps) within a test tree run, additional data will be appended to the existing file.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Slope Correction Points</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>List of Digital Gain Modes to use for slope correction. A linear regression will be used to fit a line through these points. Leave blank to use all points.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>EnhLinTx Calibration - Limits</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Enh Lin Tx Cal Limits</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Expected Min First SegmentPower</Name><Value>25</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration - Limits</ParentName><Description>Sanity Check: Expected Min Trigger Powers. Calibration will fail if trigger falls below this.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Expected Max First Segment Power</Name><Value>35</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration - Limits</ParentName><Description>Sanity Check: Expected Max Trigger Power. Calibration will fail if trigger exceeds this.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable FTM RF Mode Exit</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Enable FTM RF Mode Exit
.If this flag is enabled, GSM SW disables all RF devices</Description><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Watch for Messages ?</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Text Marker</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Any Text to Log - Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "format" part of printf. Supported printf place-holders are: %d,%f,%s; for int, double, and string. There can be many place-holders. Example entry: Marker :: c:\qcn_backup\%s. In this example "%s" will be replaced with the corresponding or equivalent key value in "Args" parameter and it will result in the corresponding marker in the log.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Marker Args</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><Description>Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "args" part of printf. A delimited list of keywords. Must have the same number of elements as the number of place-holders in "Command" param. Example entry: TESTTREEID. In this example "TESTTREEID" key will replace the "%s" found in "Command" param with the actual TESTTREEID of the tree used.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use Config Lookup For Marker Args</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><DisplayHint>1282</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable DLF Logging</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>File Name Marker</Name><Value>TEST</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><Description>File Name will be DLFLog_&lt;filenamemarker&gt;_TimeStamp.dlf. File will be stored in C:\Qualcomm\Qdart\Temp</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>List of Log Packets for DLF Logging</Name><Value>0x5082,0x5260</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls></Parameters><HIVENodeProperties>0</HIVENodeProperties></HiveProperties></HiveTest><HiveTest NodeType="Test"><Index>d7d39fc0-efe9-4fa0-8ada-dd569c836495</Index><OriginalIndex>0852ed2b-232d-42ef-af79-f74b9744878e</OriginalIndex><HiveProperties NodeType="TestProperty"><UniqueName /><UniqueNames /><AxiomMetricCSV /><LogPath /><isAxiomEdit>false</isAxiomEdit><TestName>GSM Tx Cal : PCS</TestName><RealName>RFCal_V2_GSM_Linear_Tx_Cal</RealName><Description>RF Calibration procedure that performs GSM Tx DA Calibration.

It uses FTM_DA_CAL API to perform the necessary UUT sweep.</Description><IsLinkActive xsi:nil="true" /><NodeRID>-1</NodeRID><NumberOfTests>1</NumberOfTests><Parameters><ParameterCls><Name>RF Mode</Name><Value>12</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Phone RF Mode</Description><Constraints>CDMA_800=5;CDMA_1900=6;CDMA_1800=8;J_CDMA=14;CDMA_450=17;CDMA_IMT=19;CDMA_1900_EXT=26;CDMA_450_EXT=27;CDMA_BC15=32;CDMA_800_SEC=33;WCDMA_IMT(BC1)=9;WCDMA_1900B(BC2)=16;WCDMA_800_Gen(BC5)=22;WCDMA_1800(BC3)=25;WCDMA_(BC4)=28;WCDMA_(BC8)=29;WCDMA_(BC9)=31;WCDMA_1500(BC11)=40;WCDMA_(BC19)=75;GSM_900=10;GSM_1800=11;GSM_1900=12;GSM_850=18;LTE_B1=34;LTE_B7=35;LTE_B13=36;LTE_B17=37;LTE_B38=38;LTE_B40=39;LTE_B11=41;LTE_B4=42;LTE_B2=43;LTE_B3=44;LTE_B5=45;LTE_B6=46;LTE_B8=47;LTE_B9=48;LTE_B10=49;LTE_B12=50;LTE_B14=51;LTE_B15=52;LTE_B16=53;LTE_B18=54;LTE_B19=55;LTE_B20=56;LTE_B21=57;LTE_B22=58;LTE_B23=59;LTE_B24=60;LTE_B25=61;LTE_B26=62;LTE_B27=63;LTE_B28=64;LTE_B29=65;LTE_B30=66;LTE_B31=67;LTE_B32=68;LTE_B33=69;LTE_B34=70;LTE_B35=71;LTE_B36=72;LTE_B37=73;LTE_B39=74;LTE_B41=76;LTE_B42=77;LTE_B43=88;LTE_B39_B=78;LTE_B45=79;LTE_B46=89;LTE_B47=95;LTE_B48=96;LTE_B71=97;LTE_B38_K=98;LTE_B67=99;LTE_B68=121;LTE_B49=122;LTE_B250=94;LTE_B252=80;LTE_B255=82;LTE_B66=83;TDSCDMA_B34=90;TDSCDMA_B39=91;TDSCDMA_B40=92;LTE_B72=123;LTE_B73=124;LTE_B85=125;LTE_B86=156;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Block Mask</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Block Mask. Bit0 = block A , Bit 1= block B as so on...</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NV Mode</Name><Value>12</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Phone NV Mode. Not necessarily the same as "RF Mode". Denotes the se