unction</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:AMPM Smoothing Knot</Name><Value>2</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>AMPM Smoothing Knot, unit dBDAC. An input to the spline smoothing function</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Calibration RGI When DA Calibration Skipped</Name><Value>25</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>If DA Calibration is skipped this RGI is used to generated the predistortion calibration waveform</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Step Duration</Name><Value>200</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: Time Intervals. Controls how long the DAC is held at the same value by the UUT. A segment length of 1 corresponds to 3.692 microsecs, which is 1 Time Interval.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Measurement Offset</Name><Value>112</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: uS. It delays "DA:Measurement Length" from taking effect once trigger occurs. Default: 112 us.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Measurement Length</Name><Value>100</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: uS. Controls how long of each segment is measured.Default: 250 uS. Do not go lower as since some equipment may not support.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Trigger DAC List</Name><Value>10000</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>List of Trigger DACs, these form the beginning of the waveform and are not used as measurements</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Measurement DAC List</Name><Value>10000</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>List of Measurement DACs. Note: This list must be monotonic - increasing or decreasing.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Phase Reference DAC</Name><Value>10000</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Phase refernce DAC, which will be interleaved in the waveform</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Min Limit of Max Power</Name><Value>27</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Sanity Check: Minimum Limit of Max Power measured in the calibration waveform</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Min Limit of power flatness of Adjacent Phase Reference Steps</Name><Value>0.5</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Sanity Check: Min Limit of power flatness of Phase Reference Steps</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Phase Spike Detection Threshold (degrees)</Name><Value>10</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Sanity Check: Max limit of phase between measurment steps (if larger - calibration will fail)</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQ PreDist Modem Constants OverRide</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if Modem constants need to be overriden</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NonIQPreDist:Modem Const:DAC Scaling</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Modem Constants OverRide</ParentName><Description>Digital Gain Unity parameter used to process captured IQ Data</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Dump Debug CSV</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NonIQ PreDist Calibration</ParentName><Description>Creates a csv file for Non IQ Cal debug. File saved as C:\NonIQDebug.csv.File format is DAC, F1 AMAM,F1 AMPM, F2 AMAM, F2 AMPM, F3 AMAM,F3 AMPM</Description><DisplayHint>5378</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use Debug CSV to create NV instead of measured data</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Non