<Description>Units: Time Intervals. Controls how long the RGI is held at the same value by the UUT. A segment length of 1 corresponds to 3.692 microsecs, which is 1 Time Interval.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Waveform Max Level</Name><Value>30</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: dBm. The max level in the waveform (per PA range) - used to set input level on the box</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Calibration PA Range</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Predistortion calibration will be done at this PA range.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Power of Calibation RGI</Name><Value>26.5</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: dBm. Predistortion calibration has to be performed at an RGI that corresponds to this Power.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:PA Ranges List</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Controls Tx PA gain settings for which measurements will be performed. Should be only one value per each segment to be actually calibrated. </Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:RGI List</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Controls Tx RGI gain settings for which measurements will be performed. Should be only one value per each segment to be actually calibrated. </Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Mode Param List</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Controls Mode settings for which measurements will be performed. Should be only one value per each segment to be actually calibrated. Modes 0,1 will be used for DA Cal, rest for Char Predistortion cal.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Measurement Start Delay</Name><Value>50</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: mS. The delay between arming the test equipment and the phone. Default: 0 ms.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Measurement Offset</Name><Value>50</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: uS. It delays "DA:Measurement Length" from taking effect once trigger occurs. Default: 112 us.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Measurement Length</Name><Value>100</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: uS. Controls how long of each segment is measured.Default: 250 uS. Do not go lower as since some equipment may not support.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Saturation Detection Window</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Units: dB. Applied to GMSK maxPower of PA Range 0. Example 1: Measured Power List PA0 [...,29,31,32.25,32.4,32.5] and window is 0.3, NV will be [...,29,31,32.25,32.25,32.25] Example 2: Measured Power List PA0 [...,29,31,32.25,33.4,33.8] and window is 0.3, NV will be [...,29,31,32.25,33.4,33.8]</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Modem Const:DAC Scaling</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Digital Gain Unity parameter used to process captured IQ Data</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Do Power Adaptation</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if power adaptation should be applied during calibration. This will automatically be disabled if there are no enhanced sweep points.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Do Piecewise-Linear Adaptation</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if piecewise linear adaptation should be applied during calibration.This will automatically be disabled if there are less than two enhanced sweep points.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Do Slope Correction</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if slope correction should be applied during calibration.This will automatically be disabled if there are less than two enhanced sweep points.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Slope Correction Align Low</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>When applying slope correction, set this to Enable to align the curve at the low side. Otherwise, the curve will be aligned at the high side.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Do Max Power Estimation</Name><Value>1</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if extrapalating max power estimation should be applied during calibration. </Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Output DA Char to Output File</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Determines if char DA will be written to the char XML output file.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Output File to Write GSMTxChar Data</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Complete file name with path of the GSM Tx Characterized data table genration. Use %s to specify the UUTID, %d to specify the current date, and %t to specify the current time. When generating characterization data, normal predistortion calibration (including NV writes) will be partially disabled. Leave empty to NOT generate GSM Tx Char Data and run normal calibration instead. When filenames are the same (minus timestamps) within a test tree run, additional data will be appended to the existing file.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Slope Correction Points</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>List of Digital Gain Modes to use for slope correction. A linear regression will be used to fit a line through these points. Leave blank to use all points.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>EnhLinTx Calibration - Limits</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration</ParentName><Description>Enh Lin Tx Cal Limits</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Expected Min First SegmentPower</Name><Value>25</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration - Limits</ParentName><Description>Sanity Check: Expected Min Trigger Powers. Calibration will fail if trigger falls below this.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enh Lin Tx:Expected Max First Segment Power</Name><Value>35</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Double</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>EnhLinTx Calibration - Limits</ParentName><Description>Sanity Check: Expected Max Trigger Power. Calibration will fail if trigger exceeds this.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable FTM RF Mode Exit</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Enable FTM RF Mode Exit
.If this flag is enabled, GSM SW disables all RF devices</Description><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Watch for Messages ?</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Text Marker</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Any Text to Log - Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "format" part of printf. Supported printf place-holders are: %d,%f,%s; for int, double, and string. There can be many place-holders. Example entry: Marker :: c:\qcn_backup\%s. In this example "%s" will be replaced with the corresponding or equivalent key value in "Args" parameter and it will result in the corresponding marker in the log.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Marker Args</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><Description>Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "args" part of printf. A delimited list of keywords. Must have the same number of elements as the number of place-holders in "Command" param. Example entry: TESTTREEID. In this example "TESTTREEID" key will replace the "%s" found in "Command" param with the actual TESTTREEID of the tree used.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use Config Lookup For Marker Args</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><DisplayHint>1282</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable DLF Logging</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>File Name Marker</Name><Value>TEST</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><Description>File Name will be DLFLog_&lt;filenamemarker&gt;_TimeStamp.dlf. File will be stored in C:\Qualcomm\Qdart\Temp</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>List of Log Packets for DLF Logging</Name><Value>0x5082,0x5260</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls></Parameters><HIVENodeProperties>0</HIVENodeProperties></HiveProperties></HiveTest><HiveTest NodeType="Test"><Index>3e8fe014-c363-4ba3-bf0f-4bfe43e069cd</Index><OriginalIndex>cb51af0f-32e5-4503-af42-f53fa9b4307d</OriginalIndex><HiveProperties NodeType="TestProperty"><UniqueName /><UniqueNames /><AxiomMetricCSV /><LogPath /><isAxiomEdit>false</isAxiomEdit><TestName>Check Phone Communication</TestName><RealName>RFCal_CheckPhoneCommAndPhoneMode</RealName><Description>Establish communication with phone, check/set phone mode, send key press, and other phone operations. Note that some parameters in this node are used globally, and some may be overriden by SUITEGlobalConfiguration test node. Check the individual params descriptions.</Description><IsLinkActive xsi:nil="true" /><PostCondition><Expression>C1</Expression><Conditions><BaseCondition xsi:type="TestPostCondition"><Name>C1</Name><GlobalVariableSign>Equals</GlobalVariableSign><TestConditionType>TestResult</TestConditionType><ParameterSign>Equals</ParameterSign><ParameterValue /><CompareToType>Constant</CompareToType><Result>Failed</Result><ParameterIndex>-1</ParameterIndex></BaseCondition></Conditions><Action>Branch</Action><BranchTestIndex>677c816b-ccb1-4c42-ad66-212f89decdb5</BranchTestIndex><BranchOnTestName>RFCal_QDART_FinalizeDataLogging</BranchOnTestName><BranchByTestName>false</BranchByTestName></PostCondition><Notes>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Microsoft Sans Serif;}}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs17\par
}
</Notes><NodeRID>-1</NodeRID><NumberOfTests>1</NumberOfTests><Parameters><ParameterCls><Name>Dump Start Timeout</Name><Value>120000</Value><Unit>milliseconds(ms)</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description> Min Dump Start Trigger time </Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Dump Collection Timeout</Name><Value>300000</Value><Unit>milliseconds(ms)</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description> Min Waite time for Dump Collection </Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Post Dump Collection Wait</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>milliseconds(ms)</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description> Wait time after Dump Collection </Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Post Dump collection command</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Post Dump collection command</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Phone Reset Method</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>Power On/Off</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Power On/Off</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>If Software PhoneReset is selected, the application calls the PhoneReset API to perform a phone reset. If Power On/Off is selected, the power to the phone is turned off and then turned on.WARNING: SUITEGlobalConfiguration test node can override this param.If SUITEGlobalConfiguration has not run, this param will be used globally</Description><Constraints>Power On/Off;Software PhoneReset</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Need Buildloader?</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Key Press Settings</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Click to see the options for key press settings, e.g., key press required, key press ID, etc, etc.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Keypress Required?</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Key Press Settings</ParentName><Description>WARNING: SUITEGlobalConfiguration test node can override this param.If SUITEGlobalConfiguration has not run, this param will be used globally</Description><DisplayHint>5122</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>KeyPress ID</Name><Value>81</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Key Press Settings</ParentName><Description>The Key Press ID to be sent to the phone after a phone powerUp. This parameter is valid only when the 'Send KeyPress After Phone PowerUp' is set to true in this node.WARNING: SUITEGlobalConfiguration test node can override this param.If SUITEGlobalConfiguration has not run, this param will be used globally</Description><Constraints>KEY_0=48;KEY_1=49;KEY_2=50;KEY_3=51;KEY_4=52;KEY_5=53;KEY_6=54;KEY_7=55;KEY_8=56;KEY_9=57;SEND_KEY=80;END_KEY=81;CLEAR_KEY=82;UP_ARROW_KEY=84;DOWN_ARROW_KEY=85;MENU_KEY=91;PWR_KEY=111;INFO_KEY=112;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Delay before sending the KeyPress</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>millisecs</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Key Press Settings</ParentName><Description>The delay after the phone is detected on the comm port and before sending the KeyPress. WARNING: SUITEGlobalConfiguration test node can override this param.If SUITEGlobalConfiguration has not run, this param will be used globally</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Delay after sending the KeyPress</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>millisecs</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Key Press Settings</ParentName><Description>The delay after sending the KeyPress. WARNING: SUITEGlobalConfiguration test node can override this param.If SUITEGlobalConfiguration has not run, this param will be used globally</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Num of Times to Send the KeyPress</Name><Value>1</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Key Press Settings</ParentName><Description>Some targets require sending multiple times of the key press. WARNING: SUITEGlobalConfiguration test node can override this param.If SUITEGlobalConfiguration has not run, this param will be used globally</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Total Timeout Setting</Name><Value>1800000</Value><Unit>s</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>WARNING: SUITEGlobalConfiguration. Total Timeout of every single node, including the power supply toggle delay and power on delay. Restrict the running time of every single node, especailly for phone crashed when testing. The total run time will exceed setting time if this time is very small.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Com Port Comm Wait</Name><Value>120</Value><Unit>s</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Timeout to wait for the QPST server to find an active phone. WARNING: SUITEGlobalConfiguration test node can override this param.If SUITEGlobalConfiguration has not run, this param will be used globally</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Desired Phone Mode</Name><Value>1</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>1=FTM, 0=DMSS,2=Do Not Set</Description><Constraints>DMSS=0;FTM=1;Do Not Set=2;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use Extended Phone Mode?</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>If this is checked, the "Desired Phone Mode" will be overwritten by "Extended Phone Mode"</Description><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Extended Phone Mode</Name><Value>3</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Only take effect if "Use Extended Phone Mode?" is true. </Description><Constraints>OFFLINE=1;RESET=2;FTM=3;ONLINE=4;LOW_POWER=5;POWER_OFF=6;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Just wait for the desired mode?</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Just wait for desired mode (or extended phone mode) without mode change, 1=Wait, 0=No</Description><Constraints>No wait=0;Wait without mode change=1;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Waiting for the desired Phone Mode in ms</Name><Value>60000</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Just wait for the desired mode?</ParentName><Description>Just wait for desired mode without mode change, 1=Wait, 0=No</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Force Phone Mode</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Even if the phone is already in the desired phone mode, the "Set Phone Mode" command will still be issued.</Description><Constraints>No;Yes</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Change Boot Mode</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Valid only for FTM/DMSS modes. If this is checked, the NV ID NV_FTM_MODE_I will be checked against the desired mode. If not match, a NV write and phone reset will be performed. The FTM/DMSS runtime switching Diag command will not be used.</Description><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Delay before setting PhoneMode</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>s</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Delay before setting the phone mode and after detecting the phone on the communications port</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Max Number of Attempts</Name><Value>3</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Max number of attempts. Power supply will be cycled off and on between each attempt. WARNING: SUITEGlobalConfiguration test node can override this param.If SUITEGlobalConfiguration has not run, this param will be used globally</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Disallow Reset Mobile</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>If this is checked, no reset mobile will be allowed in this node, and the nodes within the same Init/Finalize Data Logging scope.
Note: this param do not obey the SUITE Global configuration.</Description><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Multi-Phone</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Click to see the options for multiple active phone settings.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Check All Expected Active Phones</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Multi-Phone</ParentName><Description>Valid only when AddActivePhone was run prior to this node, if multiple active phones were detected on comports and added by AddActivePhone, this flag decides if all phones comport port connection should be established and phone mode set to the desired mode</Description><DisplayHint>5122</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Primary Phone Technology</Name><Value>-1</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Multi-Phone</ParentName><Description>Valid only for multiple active phones concurrency, when "Check All Expected Active Phones" is Yes. if multiple active phones were detected on comports and added by AddActivePhone, this flag decides which phone is the primary phone. -1 is auto detect, based on the name of DLL.</Description><Constraints>SameAsDLLName=-1;CDMA=0;WCDMA=1;GSM=2;BlUETOOTH=3;MEDIAFLO=4;DVBH=5;ANALOG=6;GPS=7;ISDBT=8;1xEVDO=9;LTE=10;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Require Other Phones Active</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Multi-Phone</ParentName><Description>Valid only for multiple active phones concurrency. if multiple active phones were detected on comports and added by AddActivePhone, this flag decides if all UPCOMING TEST NODES should ensure all phones active at the same time. If detected lost phone, power supply will be toggled to bring back all phones.Note that this param takes effect only when "Check All Expected Active Phones" is true.</Description><DisplayHint>5122</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Phone Mode Of Other Phones</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Multi-Phone</ParentName><Description>Valid only for multiple active phones concurrency, when "Check All Expected Active Phones" is Yes.if multiple active phones were detected on comports and added by AddActivePhone, this flag decides if all the other phone should be set to FTM/LPM mode if the desired mode of current phone is Online.</Description><Constraints>DoNotSet=-1;Same=0;FTM=1;LPM=2;ReverseOnlineFTM=3;ReverseOnlineLPM=4;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable Multi Phone Auto Detection</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Multi-Phone</ParentName><Description>Valid only for multiple active phones concurrency, when "Check All Expected Active Phones" is Yes, the RF HW config NV will be read, and if the target should appear as multiple comports, the comports will be scaned and the comport number will be added.
NOTE: by default, the RFCal DLL does not honor this parameter. To use auto detection in RFCal DLL, please check "Override Code"</Description><DisplayHint>5122</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Override Code</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Multi-Phone</ParentName><Description>Valid only in RFCal DLL. To use auto detection in RFCal DLL, this flag must be checked.</Description><Constraints>None=0;AllowAutoDetectionInRFCalDLL=1;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Phone Reset Count Statistics</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Click to see the options for phone reset count statistics.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Phone Reset Count Stat Max Limit: General</Name><Value>999</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Phone Reset Count Statistics</ParentName><Description>This max limit will apply to the phone reset count for reset purpose of General. If the reset count exceeds this limit, the phone reset count statistics test will be marked as a failure.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Phone Reset Count Stat Max Limit: Lost Diag</Name><Value>999</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Phone Reset Count Statistics</ParentName><Description>This max limit will apply to the phone reset count for reset purpose of Lost Diag. If the reset count exceeds this limit, the phone reset count statistics test will be marked as a failure.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Phone Reset Count Stat Max Limit: Refresh NV</Name><Value>999</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Phone Reset Count Statistics</ParentName><Description>This max limit will apply to the phone reset count for reset purpose of Refresh NV. If the reset count exceeds this limit, the phone reset count statistics test will be marked as a failure.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Phone Reset Count Stat Max Limit: Force Registration</Name><Value>999</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Phone Reset Count Statistics</ParentName><Description>This max limit will apply to the phone reset count for reset purpose of Force Registration. If the reset count exceeds this limit, the phone reset count statistics test will be marked as a failure.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Phone Reset Count Stat Max Limit: Call Failure</Name><Value>999</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Phone Reset Count Statistics</ParentName><Description>This max limit will apply to the phone reset count for reset purpose of Call Failure. If the reset count exceeds this limit, the phone reset count statistics test will be marked as a failure.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Phone Reset Count Stat Max Limit: Measurement Failure</Name><Value>999</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Phone Reset Count Statistics</ParentName><Description>This max limit will apply to the phone reset count for reset purpose of Measurement Failure. If the reset count exceeds this limit, the phone reset count statistics test will be marked as a failure.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Phone Reset Count Stat Max Limit: Registration Failure</Name><Value>999</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Phone Reset Count Statistics</ParentName><Description>This max limit will apply to the phone reset count for reset purpose of Registration Failure. If the reset count exceeds this limit, the phone reset count statistics test will be marked as a failure.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Phone Reset Count Stat Max Limit: Unknown</Name><Value>999</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Phone Reset Count Statistics</ParentName><Description>This max limit will apply to the phone reset count for reset purpose of Unknown. If the reset count exceeds this limit, the phone reset count statistics test will be marked as a failure.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Watch for Messages ?</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Text Marker</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Any Text to Log - Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "format" part of printf. Supported printf place-holders are: %d,%f,%s; for int, double, and string. There can be many place-holders. Example entry: Marker :: c:\qcn_backup\%s. In this example "%s" will be replaced with the corresponding or equivalent key value in "Args" parameter and it will result in the corresponding marker in the log.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Marker Args</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><Description>Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "args" part of printf. A delimited list of keywords. Must have the same number of elements as the number of place-holders in "Command" param. Example entry: TESTTREEID. In this example "TESTTREEID" key will replace the "%s" found in "Command" param with the actual TESTTREEID of the tree used.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use Config Lookup For Marker Args</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><DisplayHint>1282</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable DLF Logging</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>File Name Marker</Name><Value>TEST</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><Description>File Name will be DLFLog_&lt;filenamemarker&gt;_TimeStamp.dlf. File will be stored in C:\Qualcomm\Qdart\Temp</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>List of Log Packets for DLF Logging</Name><Value>0x5082,0x5260</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls></Parameters><HIVENodeProperties>0</HIVENodeProperties></HiveProperties></HiveTest><FolderProperties NodeType="FolderProperty"><UniqueName /><UniqueNames /><AxiomMetricCSV /><LogPath /><isAxiomEdit>false</isAxiomEdit><Expanded>true</Expanded><TestName>GSM Tx</TestName><RealName>Folder</RealName><IsLinkActive xsi:nil="true" /><Notes>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Microsoft Sans Serif;}}
