/Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>Disable</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>Disable</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Determines if NV should be logged to XML output, completely independent of NV writing.</Description><Constraints>Disable;Enable</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Rx Chain ID Selection</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Specify which Rx chain to calibrate.
0 - use C0
2 - use C2
NOTE: must enable Write New Chain Enumerated NV to use C2
</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Rx Antenna Path Selection</Name><Value>65535</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Specify which Rx antenna path to calibrate. Use only with Set Device and SigPath version V1.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Set Device and SigPath</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Specify whether to Set RFM Path: 0 - Do not set RFM Path, 1 - Set Device and Sig Path Only, 2 - Set complete RFM path, 3 - Set RFM Path V2</Description><Constraints>False=0;V1=1;V2=2;V3=3;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable DC Offset Cal</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Enable DC Offset Cal
.If this flag is enabled, Rx DC offset values are measured.</Description><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Write New Chain Enumerated NV</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Flag to specify whether to write to legacy NV or New Chain Enumerated (C0,C2 etc) NV</Description><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Write to Consolidated NV</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Flag to specify whether to write to legacy NV or consolidated Rx NV</Description><Constraints>False=0;V1=1;V2=2;V3=3;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Obtain NV Container from UUT</Name><Value>1</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>false - write Rx NV data to container specified by "Rx Chain ID Selection"true  - write Rx NV data to container specified by the UUT</Description><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Obtain Consolidated NV Data from UUT</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>false - do not read consolidated Rx NV data from UUT"true  - Read consolidated Rx NV data from UUT. Cal results will be overwritten.</Description><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Alternate Path</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>The path to use for alternate path cal.A non-zero value enables alternate path cal.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>RxDiversity</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Perform Rx Diversity Cal</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>RxDiversity</ParentName><Description>false - dont do diversitytrue - do diversityNOTE: must enable Write New Chain Enumerated NV for this cal
</Description><DisplayHint>5378</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use Main(PRx) and Aux(DRx) Ports</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>RxDiversity</ParentName><Description>false - uses the Main Port for PRx/DRx chain cal.true  - uses Main Port for PRx and Aux Port for DRx.</Description><DisplayHint>5378</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DRx-only cal on Main Port</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>RxDiversity</ParentName><Description>false - calibrates both PRx and DRx.true  - calibrates DRx only on the Main Port.</Description><DisplayHint>5378</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DRx-only cal on Aux Port</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>RxDiversity</ParentName><Description>false - calibrates both PRx and DRx.true  - calibrates DRx only on the Aux Port.</Description><DisplayHint>5378</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>HighLinearity</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>GSM High Linearity ITEMS ROOT</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>High Linearity Cal Enable</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>HighLinearity</ParentName><Description>If yes, performs High Linearity Rx Cal.</Description><DisplayHint>5122</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>High Linearity Gain Ranges</Name><Value>0,1,2,3</Value><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>HighLinearity</ParentName><Description>List of LNA states to conduct high linearity mode calibration. Valid range - 0 to 3. Max of 4 states.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>High Linearity Channel</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>HighLinearity</ParentName><Description>Channel at which high linearity mode RX calibration is done</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>HiLin:Rx Gain Offset Limits</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>HighLinearity</ParentName><Description>High linearity limits ITEMS ROOT</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>High Linearity Gain Offsets Max Limits</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>HiLin:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each high linearity rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "High Linearity Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>High Linearity Gain Offsets Min Limits</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>HiLin:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each high linearity rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "High Linearity Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>High Linearity Gain Offsets Max Limits (DRx)</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>HiLin:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each high linearity rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "High Linearity Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>High Linearity Gain Offsets Min Limits (DRx)</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>HiLin:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each high linearity rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "High Linearity Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>GSM Rx FreqComp ITEMS ROOT</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Gain Ranges</Name><Value>0,1,2,3</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp</ParentName><Description>The Rx Gain Ranges for which rx cal is performed.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Levels</Name><Value>-90,-90,-54,-54</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp</ParentName><Description>Units: dBm. The levels for which rx cal is performed. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Burst Averages</Name><Value>5</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp</ParentName><Description>Default = 5. Controls the number of bursts included in the RSSI figure reported.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Reduced Gain Range Measurement?</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp</ParentName><Description>Flag to do calibration measurements on one channel across gain ranges, and max of two gain ranges across channels and extrapolate to determine other channel/gain range measurements</Description><DisplayHint>5122</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Extrapolation Channel</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Reduced Gain Range Measurement?</ParentName><Description>Gain measured on all Gain Ranges in this Channel. Has to be one of the cal channels</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Measured Gain Ranges</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Reduced Gain Range Measurement?</ParentName><Description>Gain Measured on all channels in these Gain Ranges. Note: that the first of these is used as the reference to extrapolate the non measured data</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Output File to Append GSMRxChar Data</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp</ParentName><Description>Complete file name with path of the GSM Rx Characterized data table genration. Leave empty to NOT generate GSM Rx Char Data.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Use Characterized Data?</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp</ParentName><Description>Flag to do calibration measurements on one channel across gain ranges, and apply to characterized data to generate GSM Rx Freq Comp Data</Description><DisplayHint>5122</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Measurement Channel</Name><Value>128</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Use Characterized Data?</ParentName><Description>Gain measured on all Gain Ranges in this Channel. Has to be one of the cal channels</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:PRx Path Association</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Use Characterized Data?</ParentName><Description>Format - Sig Path1,Ant Path1;Sig Path2,Ant Path2...</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:DRx Path Association</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Use Characterized Data?</ParentName><Description>Format - Sig Path1,Ant Path1;Sig Path2,Ant Path2...</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp</ParentName><Description>FreqComp limits ITEMS ROOT</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offsets Max Limits</Name><Value>2470,2480,2260,1842</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offsets Min Limits</Name><Value>1000,1000,1000,1000</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offsets Max Limits (DRx)</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offsets Min Limits (DRx)</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable FTM RF Mode Exit</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Enable FTM RF Mode Exit
.If this flag is enabled, GSM SW disables all RF devices</Description><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Watch for Messages ?</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Text Marker</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Any Text to Log - Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "format" part of printf. Supported printf place-holders are: %d,%f,%s; for int, double, and string. There can be many place-holders. Example entry: Marker :: c:\qcn_backup\%s. In this example "%s" will be replaced with the corresponding or equivalent key value in "Args" parameter and it will result in the corresponding marker in the log.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Marker Args</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><Description>Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "args" part of printf. A delimited list of keywords. Must have the same number of elements as the number of place-holders in "Command" param. Example entry: TESTTREEID. In this example "TESTTREEID" key will replace the "%s" found in "Command" param with the actual TESTTREEID of the tree used.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use Config Lookup For Marker Args</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><DisplayHint>1282</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable DLF Logging</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>File Name Marker</Name><Value>TEST</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><Description>File Name will be DLFLog_&lt;filenamemarker&gt;_TimeStamp.dlf. File will be stored in C:\Qualcomm\Qdart\Temp</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>List of Log Packets for DLF Logging</Name><Value>0x5082,0x5260</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls></Parameters><HIVENodeProperties>0</HIVENodeProperties></HiveProperties></HiveTest><HiveTest NodeType="Test"><Index>eb4f5c16-fa14-49e8-b7ae-9494ec4b86d2</Index><OriginalIndex>d7dfc9f5-3444-4e4b-a21d-032aa721fd03</OriginalIndex><HiveProperties NodeType="TestProperty"><UniqueName /><UniqueNames /><AxiomMetricCSV /><LogPath /><isAxiomEdit>false</isAxiomEdit><TestName>GSM Rx Cal : EGSM</TestName><RealName>RFCal_V2_GSM_Rx_Cal</RealName><Description>RF Calibration procedure that performs GSM Rx Calibration.</Description><IsLinkActive xsi:nil="true" /><Notes>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Microsoft Sans Serif;}}
