 elements as "High Linearity Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>GSM Rx FreqComp ITEMS ROOT</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Gain Ranges</Name><Value>0,1,2,3</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp</ParentName><Description>The Rx Gain Ranges for which rx cal is performed.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Levels</Name><Value>-90,-90,-54,-54</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp</ParentName><Description>Units: dBm. The levels for which rx cal is performed. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Burst Averages</Name><Value>5</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp</ParentName><Description>Default = 5. Controls the number of bursts included in the RSSI figure reported.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Reduced Gain Range Measurement?</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp</ParentName><Description>Flag to do calibration measurements on one channel across gain ranges, and max of two gain ranges across channels and extrapolate to determine other channel/gain range measurements</Description><DisplayHint>5122</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Extrapolation Channel</Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Reduced Gain Range Measurement