h2,Ant Path2...</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:DRx Path Association</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Use Characterized Data?</ParentName><Description>Format - Sig Path1,Ant Path1;Sig Path2,Ant Path2...</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp</ParentName><Description>FreqComp limits ITEMS ROOT</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offsets Max Limits</Name><Value>2800,2550,2300,2000</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offsets Min Limits</Name><Value>1801,1600,1400,1200</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offsets Max Limits (DRx)</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offsets Min Limits (DRx)</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable FTM RF Mode Exit</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Enable FTM RF Mode Exit
.If this flag is enabled, GSM SW disables all RF devices</Description><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Watch for Messages ?</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Text Marker</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Any Text to Log - Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "format" part of printf. Supported printf place-holders are: %d,%f,%s; for int, double, and string. There can be many place-holders. Example entry: Marker :: c:\qcn_backup\%s. In this example "%s" will be replaced with the corresponding or equivalent key value in "Args" parameter and it will result in the corresponding marker in the log.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Marker Args</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><Description>Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "args" part of printf. A delimited list of keywords. Must have the same number of elements as the number of place-holders in "Command" param. Example entry: TESTTREEID. In this example "TESTTREEID" key will replace the "%s" found in "Command" param with the actual TESTTREEID of the tree used.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use Config Lookup For Marker Args</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><DisplayHint>1282</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable DLF Logging</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>File Name Marker</Name><Value>TEST</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><Description>File Name will be DLFLog_&lt;filenamemarker&gt;_TimeStamp.dlf. File will be stored in C:\Qualcomm\Qdart\Temp</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>List of Log Packets for DLF Logging</Name><Value>0x5082,0x5260</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls></Parameters><HIVENodeProperties>0</HIVENodeProperties></HiveProperties></HiveTest><HiveTest NodeType="Test"><Index>6afb51c2-5d9f-4495-bc4b-643f52e2f0f8</Index><OriginalIndex>5132c440-36e7-4282-ae7a-38c00ca1d0e1</OriginalIndex><HiveProperties NodeType="TestProperty"><UniqueName /><UniqueNames /><AxiomMetricCSV /><LogPath /><isAxiomEdit>false</isAxiomEdit><TestName>GSM Rx Cal : DCS</TestName><RealName>RFCal_V2_GSM_Rx_Cal</RealName><Description>RF Calibration procedure that performs GSM Rx Calibration.</Description><IsLinkActive xsi:nil="true" /><Notes>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Microsoft Sans Serif;}}
