ath2,Ant Path2...</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:DRx Path Association</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Use Characterized Data?</ParentName><Description>Format - Sig Path1,Ant Path1;Sig Path2,Ant Path2...</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp</ParentName><Description>FreqComp limits ITEMS ROOT</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offsets Max Limits</Name><Value>2700,2540,2320,2000</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offsets Min Limits</Name><Value>1801,1600,1400,1200</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offsets Max Limits (DRx)</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offsets Min Limits (DRx)</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>FreqComp:Rx Gain Offset Limits</ParentName><Description>Applied to the converted RSSI values for each rx gain range. Must have the same number of elements as "FreqComp:Gain Ranges".</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable FTM RF Mode Exit</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Enable FTM RF Mode Exit
.If this flag is enabled, GSM SW disables all RF devices</Description><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Watch for Messages ?</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Text Marker</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Any Text to Log - Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "format" part of printf. Supported printf place-holders are: %d,%f,%s; for int, double, and string. There can be many place-holders. Example entry: Marker :: c:\qcn_backup\%s. In this example "%s" will be replaced with the corresponding or equivalent key value in "Args" parameter and it will result in the corresponding marker in the log.</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Marker Args</Name><Value /><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><Description>Supports entries in printf( format, args ) style, where its entries correspond to the "args" part of printf. A delimited list of keywords. Must have the same number of elements as the number of place-holders in "Command" param. Example entry: TESTTREEID. In this example "TESTTREEID" key will replace the "%s" found in "Command" param with the actual TESTTREEID of the tree used.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Use Config Lookup For Marker Args</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Text Marker</ParentName><DisplayHint>1282</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable DLF Logging</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>4098</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>File Name Marker</Name><Value>TEST</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><Description>File Name will be DLFLog_&lt;filenamemarker&gt;_TimeStamp.dlf. File will be stored in C:\Qualcomm\Qdart\Temp</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>List of Log Packets for DLF Logging</Name><Value>0x5082,0x5260</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Enable DLF Logging</ParentName><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls></Parameters><HIVENodeProperties>0</HIVENodeProperties></HiveProperties></HiveTest><HiveTest NodeType="Test"><Index>d8e367a4-11ef-4747-88ac-e8d0b31fe787</Index><OriginalIndex>bf645f08-00d8-424c-af24-754ecaa3dbf3</OriginalIndex><HiveProperties NodeType="TestProperty"><UniqueName /><UniqueNames /><AxiomMetricCSV /><LogPath /><isAxiomEdit>false</isAxiomEdit><TestName>GSM Rx Cal : PCS</TestName><RealName>RFCal_V2_GSM_Rx_Cal</RealName><Description>RF Calibration procedure that performs GSM Rx Calibration.</Description><IsLinkActive xsi:nil="true" /><NodeRID>-1</NodeRID><NumberOfTests>1</NumberOfTests><Parameters><ParameterCls><Name>RF Mode</Name><Value>12</Value><Unit>NONE</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Phone RF Mode</Description><Constraints>CDMA_800=5;CDMA_1900=6;CDMA_1800=8;J_CDMA=14;CDMA_450=17;CDMA_IMT=19;CDMA_1900_EXT=26;CDMA_450_EXT=27;CDMA_BC15=32;CDMA_800_SEC=33;WCDMA_IMT(BC1)=9;WCDMA_1900B(BC2)=16;WCDMA_800_Gen(BC5)=22;WCDMA_1800(BC3)=25;WCDMA_(BC4)=28;WCDMA_(BC8)=29;WCDMA_(BC9)=31;WCDMA_1500(BC11)=40;WCDMA_(BC19)=75;GSM_900=10;GSM_1800=11;GSM_1900=12;GSM_850=18;LTE_B1=34;LTE_B7=35;LTE_B13=36;LTE_B17=37;LTE_B38=38;LTE_B40=39;LTE_B11=41;LTE_B4=42;LTE_B2=43;LTE_B3=44;LTE_B5=45;LTE_B6=46;LTE_B8=47;LTE_B9=48;LTE_B10=49;LTE_B12=50;LTE_B14=51;LTE_B15=52;LTE_B16=53;LTE_B18=54;LTE_B19=55;LTE_B20=56;LTE_B21=57;