</Notes><NodeRID>-1</NodeRID><NumberOfTests>1</NumberOfTests><Parameters><ParameterCls><Name>Root</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>GSM TX POut DETECTOR CAL ITEMS ROOT</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Flush NV To DUT</Name><Value>1</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Root</ParentName><Description>Indicates whether or not to flush queued NV to DUT.</Description><Constraints>No;Yes</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Flush NV Method</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Root</ParentName><Description>An integer value representing the way queued NVs are written to DUT. Applies only when "Flush NV To DUT" is true.</Description><Constraints>One-By-One=0;Batch Mode but no RF EFS NV=1;FTM RF Sequencer=2;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Clear NV Queue</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Root</ParentName><Description>Indicates whether or not to clear NV queue. Note that the queue is only cleared if no errors occur in writting nv items.</Description><Constraints>No;Yes</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Enable detailed NV write status logging</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>258</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>RF Cal Date NV Write Options</Name><Value>1</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Option to write RF Cal Date Legacy NV item to specified locations</Description><Constraints>Write to Backup QCN Only=0;Write to both Phone and QCN=1;Write to phone only=2;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Comma-separated List of Internal Cal NV Items to Write</Name><Value>5066,5067,5068,5069,5270,5271,5272,5273,25012,25013,25014,25015</Value><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Specified NV items are written into QCN file in addition to Static and Measured</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NV Tree generation option</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Option to generate NV tree using populate NV data opcode</Description><Constraints>No NV tree generation=0;Generate All Cal NV Trees=1;Tx Cal NV Tree Only=2;Rx Cal NV Tree Only=3;FBRx Cal NV Tree only=4;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>NV Tree Write command option</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Use populate NV - NV Tree Write v2 command</Description><Constraints>Use NV_TREE_WRITE_V1=0;Use NV_TREE_WRITE_V2=1;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>List of NV ID to generate on the modem</Name><Value>29618,29620,29622,29650</Value><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>NV Tree Write command option</ParentName><Description>Comma seperated NVIDs for NV_TREE_WRITE_V2</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Write RF NV Items to QCN</Name><Value /><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Writes RF NV Items to specified QCN file</Description></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Check for NV read failures</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Write RF NV Items to QCN</ParentName><Description>Check for NV read failures</Description><DisplayHint>1282</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Check Cal NV tree using get path info result</Name><Value>1</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Write RF NV Items to QCN</ParentName><Description>Check cal NV exists for each of RFM path using get path info result</Description><Constraints>Do not show=0;Check RFM path=1;Show Error if any missing path=2;</Constraints><DisplayHint>8</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Request Seperate ModemOnly QCN</Name><Value>0</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><Description>Save the calibrated modem related Nv items to a seperate (modem) qcn, Yes/No</Description><DisplayHint>258</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Modem QCN File path to Sync</Name><Value>/</Value><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request Seperate ModemOnly QCN</ParentName><Description>Modem QCN File path</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>XO calNV </Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>Yes(1)/No(0)</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request Seperate ModemOnly QCN</ParentName><Description>add selfcal DAC NV to the saved modem qcn, default 'yes'</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>DAC calNV </Name><Value>1</Value><Unit>Yes(1)/No(0)</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request Seperate ModemOnly QCN</ParentName><Description>add xo cal NV to the saved modem qcn, default 'yes'</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Request EFS Sync</Name><Value>1</Value><UpperLimit>No</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>No</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><DisplayHint>258</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>File path to Sync</Name><Value>/</Value><DataType>String</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request EFS Sync</ParentName><Description>Source file path</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>EFS Sync Timeout</Name><Value>10</Value><Unit>Seconds</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request EFS Sync</ParentName><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Delay before sending diag command</Name><Value>0</Value><Unit>milli-Seconds</Unit><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request EFS Sync</ParentName><Description>Delay before sending the Diag command - Sync to EFS.</Description><DisplayHint>1024</DisplayHint></ParameterCls><ParameterCls><Name>Number of Retries</Name><Value>3</Value><UpperLimit>0</UpperLimit><LowerLimit>0</LowerLimit><DataType>Int</DataType><Type>Input</Type><ParentName>Request EFS Sync</ParentName><Description>Number of retries in case the first attempt to sync to EFS fails. 
